REALPACKET 0.2
id "hpylori-1983-association"
epoch "1983-1984-Warren-Marshall-early-publication"
claim ASSOCIATION "Curved gastric bacteria are reproducibly associated with chronic gastritis and ulcer-linked gastric pathology"
scope "gastric biopsy association available from the early Warren-Marshall observational and culture programme"

gate C PASS
gate E PASS
gate P PASS
gate R PASS

axis W 0.50 "Histology and early culture produce real organism-level contact, but the strong causal ulcer claim is not yet licensed"
axis N 0.50 "Histology, biopsy/culture and clinical association provide partially distinct routes"
axis I 0.50 "Association survives simple contaminant stories but causal direction and bystander alternatives remain live"
axis T 0.25 "Early evidence is concentrated in one clinical programme and limited patient contexts"
axis D 0.75 "Culture, controls, treatment response, volunteer studies and epidemiology provide clear prospective defeat routes"

generator STRUCTURAL "Contaminant, harmless-commensal, secondary-colonizer, acid/stress-primary-cause and infectious-cause rivals"
rival LIVE "Bacteria are harmless commensals or secondary colonizers of already diseased mucosa"
rival LIVE "Acid/stress/lifestyle remain primary ulcer-causation frameworks"
residue HIGH "Association is stronger than causal identification at this epoch"
mystery OPEN "Why the organism is present and whether it is causally primary remain unresolved"
ontic HOLD "Bacterial presence is not yet equivalent to an established causal ulcer mechanism"
successor VULNERABLE
shock "later-treatment-volunteer-epidemiology" PRESERVE "Later intervention and epidemiology preserve the organism-level claim and greatly strengthen causal authority"
source "Warren & Marshall early Lancet reports, 1983-1984"
source "Nobel Prize 2005 historical summary"
